## About me / Why this notebook

I have not always loved robotics. It is not something I started liking as a child. It is a career I discovered.

I fell in love with robotics in SS2 at Federal Girls' College Ezzamgbo. My school had a robotics club after the federal government, in partnership with Coderina and LEGO, set up robotics clubs in Federal Unity Colleges across Nigeria.
That was how I joined. I went to competitions with the club, and we won. By my finals, I was robotics president and the best in robotics in my set.

I did not initially want to study mechatronics, but I guess faith brought me here. I am a third-year mechatronics engineering student, and I am still discovering robotics from scratch. Club robotics and this degree are not the same thing.

I am not the smartest and not the dumbest. I am simply a girl in motion. A moving person will meet her luck.

I started backend development in 2024, then technical writing toward the end of that year. I love backend. It helps me think. 
I also took a system design course, but I only know it in theory. I have had to learn with unreliable electricity and few amenities at school but things are changing drastically.
I am still here.

Early in September 2026, I asked myself: if I want to do a master's in robotics, why not start now? It would also help me find my way through university. For a while I thought leaving backend meant I was a loser. 
Mentors and friends helped me see that navigation and pivoting are part of being human.

This repo is that start. I have a 24-week robotics learning plan. These pages are the public notebook for that plan: what I study, what I get wrong, and what finally makes sense.
